WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.391
Session guarantees describe what one client should
experience Monotonic reads prevent that client

00:00:06.391 --> 00:00:08.829
from moving back to an older version.

00:00:08.829 --> 00:00:09.883
Monotonic reads.

00:00:09.883 --> 00:00:15.879
Read-your-writes is also broken if version 8
represented that client’s own completed write.

00:00:15.879 --> 00:00:22.204
Read a newly saved profile on one replica, switch
replicas, and identify the violated guarantee.

00:00:22.204 --> 00:00:29.131
For one key replicated N times, a write may wait for
W acknowledgements and a read for R responses

00:00:29.131 --> 00:00:31.675
If R+W>N, the selected sets overlap.

00:00:31.675 --> 00:00:35.350
New writes cannot obtain all three acknowledgements.

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:41.782
Reads may still obtain one response, subject to the
system’s consistency and failure rules.

00:00:41.804 --> 00:00:48.170
Linearizability makes each operation appear to take
effect at one instant between its invocation and

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:54.536
completion Its operation order must respect real-
time precedence: when one operation finishes before

00:00:54.536 --> 00:00:58.546
another begins, the later operation cannot be placed
before it.

00:00:58.546 --> 00:01:04.531
No, unless a later intervening operation legally
restored that value; the completed write must

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:05.995
precede the later read.
